Hi all,

(Maintainers of packages that depend on plyr have also been bcc'd)

This is just a quick heads up that I'm working on a updated version of
plyr that I plan to release in the next couple of months. There are no
new major changes, but I've fixed many of the small issues that have
accumulated in the last year since a major release. Since there are
now 107 packages that depend on plyr, there well be an extended RC
period to make sure that I don't accidentally break a lot of existing
code. When plyr is essentially finished and ready to upload to CRAN,
I'll give you a more formal warning, and there'll be a one month delay
before it actually goes on cran.

However, now is a good time to try out the development version and let
me know if have you any problems.  It's easiest to get it with
devtools:

library(devtools)
install_github("plyr")

Please let me know if you have any problems (esp. old code that no
longer works), any other comments or any feature requests.

Thanks!

Hadley

