Then this next line killed RStudio after about 20 seconds and no message. I tried it again in RGui and got "R for Windows GUi front-end has stopped working. A problem caused the program to stop working correctly. WIndows will close teh program and notify you if a solution is available."

ddply(myDF[myvars], .(gender), myscale)

Just for variety I also ran this, which generated odd results before that Hadley said was a bug. This killed RStudio in the same way:

myvars <- c("score")
ddply(myDF[myvars], "myDF$gender", scale)

Thanks,
Bob

